{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.LobNearZero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.LobNearZero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSincNearZero","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevReflectionTrapezoid","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.FunctionSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.NegMulLog","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrability.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_Lob_sub_near_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_Lob_sub_near_zero","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LobNearZero.lean#L143-L204","doc":"**Λ near zero, with its constant:** `|Λ(b) − (b − b·log(2b))| ≤ b³/3`\nfor `0 < b ≤ 1`.\n\nThis is the ingredient gap (A) was missing.  Everything else in the Kashaev\nexpansion is bookkeeping over Euler–Maclaurin and Stirling; this is where the\n`−½log(2N sin θ)` constant comes from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_logSinc_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_logSinc_eq","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LobNearZero.lean#L115-L139","doc":"**`∫_a^b logSinc = (Λ(a) − Λ(b)) − (b log 2b − b − (a log 2a − a))`**\nfor `0 < a ≤ b < π`.  This is the FTC step with the singular part removed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuousOn_logSinc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuousOn_logSinc","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LobNearZero.lean#L106-L113","doc":"`logSinc` is continuous on any `[a,b] ⊂ (0, π)` — it is differentiable\nthere (`hasDerivAt_logSinc`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_log_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_log_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LobNearZero.lean#L89-L104","doc":"**`∫_a^b log(2t) dt = b·log(2b) − b − (a·log(2a) − a)`** for `0 < a ≤ b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_two_sin_eq_logSinc_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_two_sin_eq_logSinc_add","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LobNearZero.lean#L80-L87","doc":"**`log(2 sin t) = logSinc t + log(2t)`** on `(0, π)`.  Both `log`s split\nbecause `sin t > 0` and `t > 0` there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LobNearZero.lean#L74-L76","doc":"**`Λ` is continuous.**  `Λ(t) = Cl₂(2t)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_Cl_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_Cl_2","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LobNearZero.lean#L56-L72","doc":"**`Cl₂` is continuous**, by the Weierstrass M-test against `∑ 1/(k+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}